## 📝 Adding Blog Posts

Blog posts are managed in `lib/blog.ts`. To add a new post:

1. Add a new object to the `blogPosts` array:

```typescript
{
  id: 4,
  title: 'Your Post Title',
  excerpt: 'Short description',
  category: 'Budgeting',
  date: 'January 20, 2024',
  readTime: '5 min read',
  image: 'https://images.unsplash.com/...',
  content: `<p>Your HTML content here</p>`,
}
```

2. The post will automatically appear on the blog page and be accessible via `/blog/4`

## 🚢 Deployment

### Deploy to Vercel (Recommended)

1. Push your code to GitHub
2. Connect your GitHub repository to Vercel
3. Vercel will automatically detect Next.js and deploy
4. Configure your domain in Vercel dashboard

```bash
# Or deploy directly with Vercel CLI
npm i -g vercel
vercel
```

### Deploy to Other Platforms

This Next.js app can be deployed to any platform that supports Node.js:
- Netlify
- Railway
- Render
- AWS Amplify
- Google Cloud Run

## 🔒 Environment Variables

Create a `.env.local` file for local development:

```env
# Email Configuration (Optional)
SMTP_HOST=your_smtp_host
SMTP_PORT=587
SMTP_USER=your_email
SMTP_PASS=your_password

# Analytics (Optional)
NEXT_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_ANALYTICS_ID=your_ga_id
```

